/**
 * NOT emitted by `kn-next create` — the scaffolder only walks
 * `templates/app/`. Staged into the build context at `kn-next build` /
 * `deploy` / `preview` time instead, only when the standalone shape is
 * selected (`stageStandaloneBuildContext`, `templates/runtime-standalone/`,
 * paired with `Dockerfile.standalone.hbs`) — that CLI-selection wiring has
 * landed and is exercised by the docker-e2e suites in this package.
 *
 * knext STANDALONE supervisor entry (ADR-0055).
 *
 * This is the image's ENTRYPOINT for the node/bun STANDALONE runtime shape. Per
 * ADR-0055 the image declares how to start itself: the operator selects image +
 * env + probes and leaves the container Command `nil`, so THIS file — not a
 * command string the operator invents — is what boots the app.
 *
 * All it does is hand off to the runtime-agnostic supervisor
 * (`@getknext/core/internal/node-server`), which owns everything the operator's
 * forced `bun run server.js` command used to silently discard: SIGTERM
 * forwarding + awaited DB-pool drain + the grace hardcap, the eagerly-bound
 * `:9464` metrics endpoint the NetworkPolicy/PodMonitor assume, the compat-gated
 * Cache-Control preload, the Bun keep-alive guard, and the compile-cache
 * diagnostics. The supervisor spawns the REAL Next standalone `server.js`
 * (STANDALONE_SERVER_PATH, default `.next/standalone/server.js`) as a child so
 * SIGTERM can drain it before the pod goes away.
 *
 * DEPENDENCY-FREE ON PURPOSE. The Dockerfile copies this SAME file to BOTH
 * `/app/knext-entry.mjs` (the ENTRYPOINT target) AND `/app/server.js` (the R3
 * compat shim the CURRENT operator command — `bun run server.js` — names, so an
 * old-operator × new-image upgrade still reaches the supervisor). A relative
 * `import './x'` would resolve differently from those two paths, so the only
 * import here is the bare `@getknext/core` subpath, resolved from
 * `/app/node_modules`.
 *
 * Do not rename it. The Dockerfile's ENTRYPOINT and the compat-shim COPY both
 * point at this exact path.
 */
await import("@getknext/core/internal/node-server");
